    <briefdescription>
<para>Struct template representing a generic floating point constant with custom size and precision. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The floating point type (e.g., float, double). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>N</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The integral part of the constant value. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>D</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The digits of the fractional part of the constant value, as returned by <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1math_1a154910632d01b827ab1b67f309064211" kindref="member">math::den()</ref></computeroutput> (e.g. 25 for <computeroutput>1.25</computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The number of decimal digits, the scale of <computeroutput>D</computeroutput>, as returned by <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1math_1a3557a9ea7ea89e94be133fb78edcd01f" kindref="member">math::den_size()</ref></computeroutput> (e.g. 2 for <computeroutput>1.25</computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>P</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The sign of the value (1 for positive, -1 for negative). Defaults to 1.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1floating__point__constant" kindref="compound">floating_point_constant</ref></computeroutput> struct template provides a compile-time constant value of a floating point type, supporting custom size and precision. It inherits from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1op" kindref="compound">op</ref></computeroutput> directly rather than from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value__base" kindref="compound">value_base</ref>&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput>, since its value is the compile-time <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value" kindref="compound">value</ref></computeroutput> constant, and it needs no run-time storage; the struct is empty, and the literal operators create it with <computeroutput>{}</computeroutput>, without a constructor. Having no non-static floating point members, it is not a homogeneous floating point aggregate, so the <computeroutput>-Wpsabi</computeroutput> note described for <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value__base" kindref="compound">value_base</ref></computeroutput> does not apply to it, despite its empty base. On 32-bit Arm, GCC emits another note, about a change in GCC 7.1, for each function passing a <computeroutput>double</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>long double</computeroutput> constant by value, since the earlier versions computed its alignment from its static <computeroutput>double</computeroutput> members; the framework does not pass the constants by value.</para>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1floating__point__constant_1adcb16c95222c90598162fb5310bcd0f8" kindref="member">value_type</ref></computeroutput> alias, explicit conversion operator, and <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1floating__point__constant_1a0169d044ee9d39e5d1b63c0a1fc4ce95" kindref="member">get()</ref></computeroutput> accessor are provided directly by this struct. The compile-time <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1floating__point__constant_1acc11936d636a95777208dc8e50f2546f" kindref="member">epsilon</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value" kindref="compound">value</ref></computeroutput> static constants are retained, and a unary minus operator is provided to obtain the negative value as a new <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1floating__point__constant" kindref="compound">floating_point_constant</ref></computeroutput> instance. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
